      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T15:57:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I\u0027d prefer if this was calculated as part of the new combined setCurrentUniforms().\n\nThat would also allow us to simplify some of the internal state, since setCurrentUniforms() is the only place that needs to know if either batch key or uniform index changed. bindBuffer() only needs to know that it needs to bind the buffer, depending on fUseStorageBuffers, so we could combine fBatchKeyChanged and fUniformIndexChanged into a single fNeedBufferBinding field instead.\n\nThis would also mean that we can keep the call to `bindBuffer()` down below inside the `if (stateChanged)` loop, which seems less surprising to me than always calling `bindBuffer()` that may or may not actually bind.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 281,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 281,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "128f729a28de6a8d6a6fcefd0d3792fad6de8188",
